   "label": "FlipFlop (Rajput et al., ICSE 2026)",
   "reason": "FlipFlop's time and power models read 22 calibration constants that come from its own calibration program. The packaged H100 calibration measures 1 of them under the same definition, has only a differently defined counterpart for 9, and has none for 12 (including idle power and the power-versus-active-SM-count law). Filling them from another board, from defaults or by a new fit would be a different method; running FlipFlop's own calibration on the H100 would give it more calibration data than our model. So the row is not run on the H100 (decision of 3 October 2026: the row is not added after the freeze).",
